# Milestone 3: Truth & Credibility

#### In Milestone 3, students investigate why AI outputs can feel believable even when information is incomplete, biased, or missing context. Across Lessons 5 and 6, they test AI-generated information, identify patterns that create a false sense of credibility, and practice verification strategies before trusting an output.

## Milestone 3 Overview

#### **Lesson 5** is a Build Knowledge lesson where students complete station explorations to test AI credibility, notice patterns in convincing responses, and begin drafting a Trust Meter.

#### **Lesson 6** is a Develop & Critique lesson where students synthesize findings across explorations and create a Trust Meter that helps others decide when to trust AI and when to slow down and verify.

## 🧩 Project Progress

#### By the end of Milestone 3, students will complete the Trust & Credibility section of their Responsible AI Use Guide, including a visual Trust Meter and concrete user actions for verification.
